algorithms.pseudocode:
Algorithm: STEEPEST_EXCHANGE_DESCENT(S, c, x0)
Input:  M-convex set S, objective c, starting point x0 in S
Output: Certified optimal point x*

  x <- x0
  while True:
    best_val <- c . x
    best_move <- None
    for each (i, j) with i != j, x(i) > 0:
      x' <- exchangeVec(x, i, j)
      if x' in S and c . x' < best_val:
        best_val <- c . x'
        best_move <- (i, j, x')
    if best_move = None:
      return x  // locally optimal => globally optimal (Theorem 3.3)
    x <- best_move.x'

Complexity: O(n^2 * |S|) total, at most |S| iterations.
